            "Flip a form that shades dark or thickens to the wrong side."),
        "form-weld|Merge" => T(key, "Merge Faces", "Join the selected faces into one, or remove the selected inner edges and join the faces either side.", "Start: two faces", "Result: one face",
            "1. Select faces or inner edges.\n2. Choose Merge.",
            "Merge to tidy edge flow after splitting.", "form-merge"),
        "form-weld|Unweld edges" => T(key, "Unweld Edges", "Split the form along the selected edges so each side can move on its own.", "Start: one form", "Result: split along the edges",
            "1. Select the edges to split along.\n2. Choose Unweld edges.\n3. Move the sides apart with Edit.",
            "Weld joins them again.", "form-unweld"),
        "check|Check Cage" => Words(key, "Check Cage", "Check the cage's topology: manifold edges, face winding, degenerate faces and extraordinary points.",
            "1. Select the form.\n2. Choose Check Cage.\n3. Read the report and fix what is flagged.",
            "Fix problems before converting to NURBS."),
        "form-nurbs|Convert fewer faces" => T(key, "Convert Fewer Faces", "Convert to NURBS with one fitted patch per irregular face instead of four: a lighter solid, a little less exact near poles.", "Start: a form", "Result: a lighter NURBS solid",
            "1. Select the form.\n2. Choose Convert fewer faces.",
            "Lighter solids are quicker for booleans and fillets.", "form-smooth-surface"),
        "chamfer|Bevel" => T(key, "Bevel", "Bevel the selected cage edges: flat, or tight with support loops either side.", "Start: a sharp edge", "Result: a beveled edge",
            "1. Select edges.\n2. Choose Bevel.\n3. Set the type and width in the panel.",
            "Support loops keep the smooth surface tight to the edge.", "chamfer"),

        // ---- NURBS ----
        "raise-degree|Rebuild Surface" => T(key, "Rebuild Surface", "Redraw a surface as one patch with a chosen grid of control points.", "Start: a coarse patch", "Result: the same shape, new grid",
            "1. Choose Rebuild Surface.\n2. Pick the surface.\n3. Set the point counts, check the deviation, then accept.",
            "One clean patch is easier to edit and match than many small ones.", "more-control"),
        "raise-degree|Raise Degree" => T(key, "Raise Degree", "Increase the polynomial degree for smoother, more flexible surfaces without changing the shape.", "Start: a low-degree surface", "Result: the same shape, more control",
            "1. Choose Raise Degree.\n2. Pick the curve or surface.\n3. Set the new degree, then accept.",
            "Degree 3 is usual; G2 matching needs degree 3 or more.", "more-control"),

        // ---- mesh and scan ----
        "mesh-check|Print Check" => Words(key, "Print Check", "Pre-flight check before printing: watertight, fits your printer, supports and weight.",
